{
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "name": "copernicus_ems_aoi_reference",
  "description": "Curated, hand-drawn rectangular Area-of-Interest footprints used as reference/master data (ref_aoi). Every feature carries an analysis `region` (UAE-GULF, INDIA, US-LEGACY); rollups, dust corridors, AQI standards and fire freshness never combine regions. Features with `rollup_eligible: true` are reporting units: within a region they never overlap (shared edges only, ADR-12), so per-AOI counts add up without double counting. Features with `rollup_eligible: false` are event overlays (Copernicus-EMS-style footprints) used for validation only and never summed. `sub_region` groups reporting units (e.g. all UAE units roll up to UAE). EMSR-* features are Copernicus-EMS-style references, not verified activations; EMSR-CA-FIRE-2025 is retained as US-LEGACY because FIRMS is no longer requested for California. Shipped in-repo because Copernicus EMS rapid-mapping products are portal downloads, not an automated API (see ADR-09 / data-modeling ref_aoi).",
